        "original_id": "1f552529-fd41-540b-a935-b3041ba0f976",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-François Clervoy, Thomas Reiter, Daisuke Enomoto\n- Organizations: CNES, ESA, NASA, German Air Force\n- Roles: astronaut, engineer, Brigadier General, ESA Interagency Coordinator, Advisor to the Director General\n- Missions and Systems: NASA Space Shuttle missions, ISS, STS-121, Space Shuttle Discovery, Expedition 14, Soyuz TMA-9\n- Places: Frankfurt, West Germany, Star City, Moscow, Russia\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-François André Clervoy was born on 19 November 1958.\n- Thomas Arthur Reiter was born on 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Thomas Reiter is a retired European astronaut and a Brigadier General in the German Air Force.\n- On 6 July 2006, Thomas Reiter arrived at the ISS aboard Space Shuttle Discovery during mission STS-121.\n- Thomas Reiter was working as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency.\n- Daisuke Enomoto trained at Star City in Moscow, Russia, to fly with two members of Expedition 14 on Soyuz TMA-9.\n- Soyuz TMA-9 was launched on 18 September 2006.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
